ans to their specific activity levels and health needs.\",10\r\n3435,GASTO ENERGÉTICO BASAL,\"Gasto energético basal (GEB) refers to the amount of energy expended by the body while at rest in a neutrally temperate environment and in the post-absorptive state. It represents the energy required to maintain vital functions while the body is not engaged in any physical activity. This expenditure is crucial for sustaining essential physiological processes, ensuring that the body can perform necessary functions even when at rest.\",4\r\n3434,MUJER,\"The entity \"\"MUJER\"\" refers to a female individual, specifically in the context of energy expenditure, which is calculated using specific formulas. The term \"\"mujer\"\" also denotes the gender that pertains to human females, particularly in relation to basal energy expenditure. Additionally, women have increasingly participated in the labor market, which has influenced their food purchasing habits and the time allocated for food preparation. This multifaceted description highlights the biological, social, and economic aspects associated with women.\",4\r\n7804,EFECTO TERMOGÉNICO DE LOS ALIMENTOS,\"The thermic effect of food refers to the increase in metabolic rate after ingestion of a meal, accounting for approximately 10% of total energy consumed.\",1\r\n15527,TERMOGÉNESIS INDUCIDA POR LA DIETA,La termogénesis inducida por la dieta es el gasto energético asociado con la digestión y absorción de nutrientes.,1\r\n15528,GASTO POR ACTIVIDAD FÍSICA,\"El gasto por actividad física es la energía utilizada durante la actividad física, que se calcula mediante un factor de corrección aplicado al gasto energético basal.\",1\r\n15529,GASTO POR CRECIMIENTO,\"El gasto por crecimiento es el requerimiento energético adicional necesario para el crecimiento en niños, especialmente durante períodos de crecimiento acelerado.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n7633,GASTO ENERGÉ